{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/164141-oneiromachy-experiences","id":164141,"title":"Oneiromachy Experiences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-09T15:50:44-07:00","id":164141,"title":"Oneiromachy Experiences","content":"Of all the dreamwork we've dealt with in-game, dream combat has hardly come up. I'm curious to know how it's actually played out in your games. Has it been quick? Has it come down to who got to strike first? Did it run smoothly, or were there issues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T00:05:42-07:00","id":165695,"title":"","content":"It's happened a few times in my game. It's... interesting. Using Willpower as health tends to make the fights fast, especially since the dice pools on either side are pretty immense. And yeah, striking first is fairly important. If you're not at full Willpower, then it's really quite easy to be knocked out by a single lucky roll from an opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T11:15:09-07:00","id":166109,"title":"","content":"Thank you for sharing your experience; it confirms my suspicions and gives me some food for thought. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T18:25:33-07:00","id":168441,"title":"","content":"I played around with the oneiromachy rules using a solo character once, though I've never run them with an actual gaming group. My thoughts anyways:<br /> <br /> Quickness-wise, recalculating your character's combat traits can take a few minutes if you don't already know what to change and need to look it up in the book. (&quot;Wait, you mean everyone gets free armor?&quot;) STs who want to jump into dream combat without delay should either have their players figure that stuff out in advance, or be ready to tell them exactly what they need to change.<br /> <br /> So far as the combat itself, my experience was in line with Azahul's. The character I tried out was a social butterfly without much in the way of combat skills. Dreaming, she ended up with a moderately-sized dice pool. Characters with dots in Brawl or Melee will still be better off, but the playing field is evened.<br /> <br /> Combats go even faster under the GMC rules since equipment bonuses now add to damage rather than attacking dice pools. On the flip side, you do have to hit an opponent to take advantage of the extra damage, but hitting is more likely when everyone gets to use their best Power Attribute. Overall GMC dream combat favors powerful, high-Wyrd antagonists (like True Fae), since their dice pools are usually big enough to hit the PCs anyway.<br /> <br /> Figuring out what happens when someone dies could slow down play for STs using the GMC rules, since derangements no longer exist in quite the same form. (&quot;So, what happens to my PC now?&quot;) Probably the simplest conversion is to have being reduced below 0 Willpower cause a Condition, and being reduced below -4 cause a Persistent Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T13:20:40-07:00","id":169178,"title":"","content":"Which equipment bonuses would apply to dream combat, given that no equipment in the dreamspace is real and no equipment was mentioned in the original rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T17:59:51-07:00","id":169373,"title":"","content":"It's your Wyrd. I mean, outside of a few tokens (and those super-powerful dream items from Dancers in the Dusk that I currently can't remember the name of), equipment in dreams has no impact at all. However, the game explicitly mentions that attackers add their Wyrd &quot;as an equipment bonus&quot; to their attacks. Coupled with the +1-3 bonus for appropriate dramatic/thematic descriptions of attacks, you end up with all the dice you could possibly want without any need to lug a sword around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T21:29:13-07:00","id":169469,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as Azahul said. Combatants essentially do bonus damage equal to their Wyrd. That's part of the stuff I'd want to sort out before a game session (or prepare a dream combat cheat sheet for), since it's only mentioned once and buried under a lot of other text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T13:36:26-07:00","id":170998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combatants essentially do bonus damage equal to their Wyrd. </div> </div> </div>How so? You mean, when it's all rolled out the damage seems to add up to Wyrd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T19:22:33-07:00","id":171308,"title":"","content":"Kind of. After it's all rolled out, damage will never add up to <i>lower</i> than a changeling's Wyrd. Assuming they hit, and before damage gets reduced by the enemy's armor.<br /> <br /> For example, say we have a changeling with Wyrd 5, Strength 4, and Weaponry 3. Her dice pool is 7, and she takes a stab at someone, rolling 3 successes. That'd normally be just 3 damage, but since she adds her Wyrd as an equipment bonus, she does an extra 5, for a total of 8. And then since everyone receives free armor in dream combat, it'll get reduced by amount equal to her opponent's relevant Resistance Attribute.<br /> <br /> Under the pre-GMC rules, the changeling would've rolled 12 dice (since equipment bonuses added to dice pools), but dealt no extra damage if she scored any successes. So under the current rules, dreamers are less likely to hit opponents, but will deal more damage when they do. (And just for some numbers-related trivia, on average every three dice nets one success. The pre-GMC changeling would've needed a dice pool of 24 to deal as much damage as her GMC counterpart did, assuming perfectly average rolls).<br /> <br /> Either way, dream combat involves bigger math!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T02:21:36-07:00","id":171513,"title":"","content":"I should mention, I'm playing using pre-GMC rules, so in my game Wyrd has just been providing additional dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}